# Trivy ignore file
#
# One CVE / misconfig ID per line, each with the reason it is suppressed, so
# reviewers can revisit it when the upstream advisory changes. Checked against
# a full scan of the worker image on 2026-09-28 (OpenTofu 1.12.6, Packer
# 1.16.1); entries for the Terraform binary went with it (plan D5).

# AVD-DS-0002: the worker image runs as root. On purpose: the worker drops
# to a separate unprivileged UID per slot for every tool it runs (OpenTofu,
# Packer, OpenStack CLI), which needs root in the parent. See the comment in
# worker/Dockerfile and appstore_worker/job_context.py. The API image runs
# as a non-root user.
AVD-DS-0002

# Go modules vendored into OpenTofu 1.12.6, the latest release. Fixed only
# once OpenTofu ships a rebuild against the patched modules; bump TOFU_VERSION
# then and drop the entries a scan with `--ignorefile /dev/null` no longer
# shows. (Trivy reads ./.trivyignore by default, so a plain scan hides them.)
#
# golang.org/x/net (fixed in 0.55.0 / 0.56.0), x/text (0.39.0), x/mod (0.40.0):
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56852
CVE-2026-56864
CVE-2026-56865
# google.golang.org/grpc (fixed in 1.82.1 / 1.82.2 / 1.83.1): OpenTofu talks
# gRPC only to its own provider plugins over a local socket.
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf
CVE-2026-84304
CVE-2026-84445
# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh (fixed in 0.55.0): source-address restrictions from
# authorized_keys are not enforced. A server-side check; OpenTofu uses SSH
# only as a client (ssh provisioner).
CVE-2026-56854
# go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk (fixed in 1.43.0): only active when OpenTofu's
# OTEL tracing is switched on, which the worker never does.
CVE-2026-39883
# oras.land/oras-go/v2 (fixed in 2.6.2): OCI registries as provider or module
# sources. Apps get their providers from registry.opentofu.org; the worker
# configures no OCI mirror.
CVE-2026-50163
CVE-2026-85731
